  },
  "Scarcity": {
    "Explanation": "The email creates a sense of urgency by implying that there is ongoing discussion about the applicability of the comparative method to syntactic reconstruction and that opinions may be changing. It also suggests that there may be new information or perspectives worth considering."
  },
  "Authority": {
    "Explanation": "The email references standard introductions to historical linguistics as a source of the argument that the comparative method is inapplicable to syntactic reconstruction. This lends credibility to the argument by associating it with recognized institutions and experts in the field."
